  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the trace this ticket needs:\n\n1. **Error origin** \u2014 `\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\"` is generated in `pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`, inside the `PostStartHook()` function registered as `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"`. It fires when the repair goroutines (`startServiceClusterIPRepair` / `startServiceNodePortsRepair`) haven't both called `onFirstSuccess` within a 1-minute `time.After` window.\n\n2. **Propagation chain** \u2014 `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/hooks.go` runs every PostStartHook in a goroutine (`runPostStartHook`) and registers a matching `postStartHookHealthz{name: \"poststarthook/\"+name}` readyz check via `AddBootSequenceHealthChecks` (wired through `healthz.go`). That check stays failing (`errHookNotFinished`) until `entry.done` is closed, i.e., until the hook function returns \u2014 which is exactly the `informer-sync,poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` failure reported by readyz. If the hook returns a non-nil error instead, `runPostStartHook` calls `klog.Fatalf`, crashing the process.\n\n3. **The race** \u2014 with `MultiCIDRServiceAllocator` enabled (default from v1.33), `storage_core.go` wires the cluster-IP repair loop to `serviceipallocatorcontroller.NewRepairIPAddress(...)` (`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`). Its `RunUntil` blocks in a `wait.PollUntilContextCancel` loop waiting for the default `ServiceCIDR` object (name `\"kubernetes\"`) to exist before calling `onFirstSuccess`. That object is created/marked Ready by a *separate* PostStartHook, `\"start-kubernetes-service-cidr-controller\"` (`pkg/controlplane/instance.go` \u2192 `pkg/controlplane/controller/defaultservicecidr/default_servicecidr_controller.go`), which itself only runs on apiservers that already have the v1.33 code path. During a mixed-version rolling upgrade, IP allocation additionally routes through `MetaAllocator` (`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/cidrallocator.go`), which only serves allocations once the `ServiceCIDR`'s `Ready` condition is observed (`isReady`/`item.allocator.ready`) \u2014 otherwise callers get `ErrMismatchedNetwork`/`ErrNotReady` (`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/interfaces.go`, `ipallocator.go`). So on a freshly-upgraded node, the repair controller can stall waiting on ServiceCIDR readiness (a resource whose reconciliation depends on timing across the mixed-version cluster), the 1-minute deadline trips, and readyz reports the observed failure until the window closes and all nodes are on v1.33.",
